  "articleBody": "Storm water can seep into wall assemblies quietly, making it tough to know whether a quick patch will work or full tear-out is necessary. Here are signals indicating professional help is required:\n\n- Water pooled inside wall cavities: Saturated insulation or wet base plates cannot dry out without opening the wall.\n- Water from exterior runoff or compromised roofing: Contaminated storm runoff requires proper containment and selective disposal under industry standards like IICRC S500.\n- Soft, sagging, or bulging sheetrock: Wet drywall loses core structural integrity and fastener grip, creating fall hazards on ceilings.\n- Staining that expands or persistent musty odors: These indicators point to ongoing dampness and active fungal growth hidden from direct view.\n- Wet electrical boxes or wiring: Outlets and switches exposed to storm intrusion demand careful inspection and coordinated trade repairs before sheetrock goes back up.\n- Inability to verify deep wall dryness: If you do not own moisture meters to benchmark readings against unaffected dry walls, closing the wall risks trapped dampness.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps: Abraham Becerra personally oversees projects at HH Remodeling LLC, providing single-point coordination for drywall removal, drying, custom framing, and flawless texturing across Aurora and Denver. Call 303-505-0866 to schedule an on-site evaluation.",
